Do NOT wish for frostbrand, you have too many artifacts in the game, the
odds are stacked against you getting it.  If you truly want it, find an
altar and sacrifice till you're blue in the face, and you may get it
eventually.  I had great success with a rogue twoweaponing stormbringer and
a silver dagger, you could do the same with a silver saber, but stormy is a
broadsword, so you'll have to practice it a while.  Silver is important for
gehennom, so whatever you do, twoweapon the silver saber with it.  My first
wish would be blessed ?oCharging, or blessed magic marker if I already knew
charging.  Next would be GoP, a helm of telepathy, and perhaps that would be
all.  That only uses 3 wishes, you've got a miniumum 5 from the wand and 80%
of one from the lamp, so you could spend a couple on magic markers and maybe
a t-shirt (assuming the armory doesnt have one).

you might want a ring of levitation if you're paranoid, the heart can make
you levitate, but the wizard can steal it, and it would suck to drown on the
plane of water.  Still, I'd just polypile for it, or search gehennom, it's
usually fairly easy to find one.  Also, a ring of free action is good, as is
(to a much lesser extent) a ring of slow digestion.  You didn't mention a
BoH, maybe wish for one, or if you're not a packrat and can stay unburdened
without it, then don't bother.

mostly, I'd wish for a means of charging first, gloves and a helm, and then
save the rest.  A timely request for a *trice corpse is sometimes helpful on
the astral plane.  You might want to clear out most of gehennom (at least
down to orcus town) before wishing for a t-shirt, as there is a decent
chance of finding one.

Good luck, tread carefully, plan every move, and whatever you do, don't play
if you're not able to pay attention (i.e. due to sleep deprivation, tv,
etc.)

